1
00:00:01,518 --> 00:00:04,825
The Metal Breath Gets Stolen

2
00:00:07,929 --> 00:00:09,724
The Metal Breath?

3
00:00:09,724 --> 00:00:14,160
The Metal Breath is a legendary treasure from planet Machina.

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,686
I simply refuse to believe it would end up on such a minor planet...

5
00:00:16,686 --> 00:00:18,533
Me see it clearly!

6
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:22,420
Child's bracelet smelled like mighty Deus Machina!

7
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:25,884
I saw with my own eye too, Buster Gallon!

8
00:00:25,884 --> 00:00:29,876
That little earthling was commanding the Star Guardian like one of his lackeys!

9
00:00:29,876 --> 00:00:31,800
Black Hook, what I want to know is-

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,530
Call me Captain.

11
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:35,439
Ah, uh... C-Captain.

12
00:00:35,439 --> 00:00:37,600
What is it, Buster Gallon?

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,743
Ahem. What I want to know is... what do you plan to do once you get your hands on the Metal Breath?

14
00:00:42,743 --> 00:00:45,450
Hmm. Well, what would you do?

15
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:48,895
The one who holds the Metal Breath can rule over all Metal Cardbots.

16
00:00:48,895 --> 00:00:51,637
I would use that power to conquer the entire universe!

17
00:00:51,637 --> 00:00:54,121
Then we can divide it amongst us three, of course.

18
00:00:54,121 --> 00:00:55,603
That sounds fun.

19
00:00:55,603 --> 00:00:58,512
Yes. That much should be obvious.

20
00:00:58,512 --> 00:01:01,993
But that child has Blue Cop, a Star Guardian by his side!

21
00:01:01,993 --> 00:01:03,396
It will not be easy.

22
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:06,295
Is there any way around this?

23
00:01:06,295 --> 00:01:09,563
Of course there is. You can leave it to me.

24
00:01:46,765 --> 00:01:49,103
Mom! Where are the towels?!

25
00:01:49,628 --> 00:01:52,819
I told you to take them when you went upstairs!

26
00:01:52,819 --> 00:01:55,293
I'm busy cleaning! You come get them yourself!

27
00:01:55,293 --> 00:01:57,561
Augh, Mom!

28
00:01:57,686 --> 00:01:59,835
Ugh. Fine.

29
00:02:07,388 --> 00:02:10,705
Ugh. He'll become spoiled if I keep this up.

30
00:02:11,318 --> 00:02:12,973
I'll leave the towel here!

31
00:02:12,973 --> 00:02:14,615
I love you, Mom!

32
00:02:14,615 --> 00:02:15,973
Ugh. Save it.

33
00:02:16,688 --> 00:02:17,639
Hmph.

34
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:21,908
Aaaiyah!

35
00:02:22,889 --> 00:02:25,140
Aah! What kind of animals are these?!

36
00:02:26,491 --> 00:02:27,391
Take that!

37
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:29,778
What's going on?

38
00:02:30,179 --> 00:02:32,258
There's a bunch of strange mice out here!

39
00:02:32,258 --> 00:02:32,841
Huh?

40
00:02:32,841 --> 00:02:33,913
Here-

41
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,877
Uh... They must've ran downstairs!

42
00:02:36,877 --> 00:02:39,343
Honey! Be careful of the mice!

43
00:02:39,343 --> 00:02:41,893
What? Did you say mice, darling?

44
00:02:47,508 --> 00:02:49,258
Ah, feeling fresh!

45
00:02:49,258 --> 00:02:51,170
Oh, my Metal Breath!

46
00:03:27,381 --> 00:03:32,000
...uh... Heavy Iron...

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,377
...sealing... gonna seal you...

48
00:04:04,931 --> 00:04:07,247
Wha... where did it...

49
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,978
How did it get down there?

50
00:04:14,262 --> 00:04:16,721
Aaah!

51
00:04:19,824 --> 00:04:20,937
Stop right there!

52
00:04:21,956 --> 00:04:24,480
W-what's going on out here?!

53
00:04:25,478 --> 00:04:27,649
Waugh!

54
00:04:28,966 --> 00:04:32,372
The Mini Gallons have succeeded in stealing the Metal Breath.

55
00:04:32,372 --> 00:04:34,759
Although it took longer than expected.

56
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:35,658
Well done, Buster Gallon!

57
00:04:35,658 --> 00:04:37,137
Heheh. Bring it back quick!

58
00:04:38,338 --> 00:04:40,220
Hm? Good morning, Jun-

59
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:40,781
Give it back!

60
00:04:45,542 --> 00:04:47,841
HOT!

61
00:04:50,903 --> 00:04:52,442
Where are they hiding?

62
00:04:53,112 --> 00:04:55,365
What's all the ruckus this morning?

63
00:04:56,144 --> 00:04:57,887
Get back here!

64
00:04:57,992 --> 00:04:58,747
Oh!

65
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,129
Sorry, Mom!

66
00:05:00,728 --> 00:05:02,946
Oi oi! Who the heck are these guys?!

67
00:05:07,298 --> 00:05:08,141
Gotcha!

68
00:05:15,338 --> 00:05:16,954
Uh... Jun, what are you doing?

69
00:05:16,954 --> 00:05:19,605
Did you forget that we were going to do our homework together?

70
00:05:19,605 --> 00:05:22,552
That's not important right now! The Metal Breath has been st-

71
00:05:22,552 --> 00:05:24,603
Huh? Where did they go?!

72
00:05:24,603 --> 00:05:25,790
The Metal Breath...

73
00:05:25,790 --> 00:05:28,117
Stop right there!

74
00:05:28,117 --> 00:05:29,901
The Metal Breath was stolen?!

75
00:05:30,869 --> 00:05:32,882
How did this happen? Who could have done this?

76
00:05:32,882 --> 00:05:36,752
It was those little guys over there! They look like Black Hook's crewmate!

77
00:05:36,752 --> 00:05:38,235
Juuuuun!!

78
00:05:38,235 --> 00:05:39,762
I said stop!

79
00:05:44,319 --> 00:05:45,891
Just a little more!

80
00:05:53,673 --> 00:05:54,865
You almost got them, Jun!

81
00:05:55,305 --> 00:05:56,336
Stop!

82
00:05:58,158 --> 00:05:59,379
I got them!

83
00:05:59,379 --> 00:06:01,391
Way to go Anna, you're the best!

84
00:06:01,391 --> 00:06:03,490
I- wait a minute!-

85
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:05,532
Please stop it!

86
00:06:05,932 --> 00:06:08,375
I can't hold them any longer!

87
00:06:09,331 --> 00:06:10,641
Anna, are you alright?!

88
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:13,576
Ow... I'm really sorry, Jun...

89
00:06:13,576 --> 00:06:16,843
It's okay, I think we've driven them in the right direction!

90
00:06:16,843 --> 00:06:20,120
Luckily they're headed straight for Uncle Edo's car center!

91
00:06:21,281 --> 00:06:23,449
Huh? They snuck inside here?

92
00:06:23,449 --> 00:06:26,548
Yes! So please help me look for them too!

93
00:06:26,548 --> 00:06:28,500
I really need your help, guys!

94
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:34,593
What a bunch of pesky little things. Even if they did come in here, it will take some time before we find...

95
00:06:34,593 --> 00:06:36,085
...Them?

96
00:06:38,076 --> 00:06:42,000
Why they just go round and round in circle?

97
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,117
Are they broken?

98
00:06:43,117 --> 00:06:44,639
That's impossible!

99
00:06:44,639 --> 00:06:45,754
Where are they?

100
00:06:45,754 --> 00:06:48,372
A... car center just outside of Mowtown.

101
00:06:48,372 --> 00:06:49,560
Me go check on them.

102
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,548
What are you going to do?!

103
00:06:51,548 --> 00:06:52,579
Wait for me!

104
00:06:58,790 --> 00:07:01,357
Hm... I've got a bad feeling about this.

105
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:10,237
You little rats!

106
00:07:10,237 --> 00:07:11,432
Way to go!

107
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,980
Those little guys are pretty slippery!

108
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:30,629
Listen up, I have a plan.

109
00:07:57,259 --> 00:07:59,689
Aha! I got it!

110
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,331
Metal Cardbot, setup!

111
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,677
Trying to steal all of us? I'll admit, you have some guts.

112
00:08:21,677 --> 00:08:23,874
Yeah. They sure do.

113
00:08:23,874 --> 00:08:25,915
Now whattaya say we show 'em some hospitality?

114
00:08:25,915 --> 00:08:30,189
I agree. Should we make them tell us where we can find Black Hook's hideout?

115
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:34,125
They're getting away!

116
00:08:34,125 --> 00:08:36,903
I've had enough running around...

117
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:39,701
Hand over tiny trio!

118
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:41,793
Huh...?

119
00:08:42,202 --> 00:08:45,981
Buffalo Crush! Just barging in like that won't solve anything!

120
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:47,793
Huh?

121
00:08:48,368 --> 00:08:51,596
My precious little mini-mes!!

122
00:08:51,596 --> 00:08:54,721
How can this be?...

123
00:08:54,721 --> 00:08:59,831
Uh, uh... I-I dunno.

124
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:02,322
Hey! If you're here to fight, then hurry it up!

125
00:09:02,322 --> 00:09:04,567
Buffalo Crush! Let's retreat for now!

126
00:09:04,567 --> 00:09:09,980
No retreat! Me not leaving without Jun and Metal Breath!

127
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:10,288
Yaaah!!

128
00:09:10,288 --> 00:09:11,206
Buffalo Crush!

129
00:09:11,206 --> 00:09:13,394
Me get revenge for tiny trio!

130
00:09:13,394 --> 00:09:14,793
That was your fault!

131
00:09:18,831 --> 00:09:20,153
Metal Breath, pickup!

132
00:09:24,134 --> 00:09:25,442
Dexter, setup!

133
00:09:31,962 --> 00:09:34,465
Dexter, Helix Sword!

134
00:09:36,427 --> 00:09:38,432
Helix Sword!

135
00:09:45,606 --> 00:09:48,923
Let's put a hole in those axes! Spear Thrust!

136
00:09:48,923 --> 00:09:50,528
Hole?

137
00:09:50,528 --> 00:09:52,908
Spear Thrust!

138
00:09:55,904 --> 00:09:58,528
Step aside, Buffalo Crush!

139
00:10:04,586 --> 00:10:06,177
Chest Cannon!

140
00:10:10,846 --> 00:10:13,284
Buffalo Crush! We need to retreat!

141
00:10:13,284 --> 00:10:14,927
Me can still fight!

142
00:10:14,927 --> 00:10:16,452
Now is not the time!

143
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:25,514
You need to know when to call it quits, Buffalo Crush!

144
00:10:25,514 --> 00:10:27,230
Black Hook!

145
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:30,797
I'll admit, today was a defeat for the Black Crew!

146
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:32,168
Black Crew?

147
00:10:32,168 --> 00:10:33,529
B... Black Crew?

148
00:10:33,529 --> 00:10:37,100
Me not your henchman! Me hate that name!

149
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,562
And you're not black! You're blue!

150
00:10:39,562 --> 00:10:40,740
E-enough!

151
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,370
I told you to call me Captain!

152
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:45,240
-I'm staying out of this. This is getting embarassing.
-No! Put me down!

153
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:50,615
Ahem. Anyways! The legacy of Deus Machina will be mine!

154
00:10:50,615 --> 00:10:52,591
Deus Machina's legacy?

155
00:10:52,591 --> 00:10:54,932
If you mean the Metal Breath, that's a misunderstanding!

156
00:10:54,932 --> 00:10:57,537
And why should I believe you?

157
00:11:07,883 --> 00:11:10,514
Ah! All done.

158
00:11:10,514 --> 00:11:13,379
Hey Wild Guardy, your sword is as good as-

159
00:11:13,379 --> 00:11:15,301
Ahaha... thank goodness...!

160
00:11:15,301 --> 00:11:16,975
Right? Yeah!

161
00:11:16,975 --> 00:11:18,769
Hey, kids?

162
00:11:18,769 --> 00:11:22,360
Uncle Edo!

163
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,735
Would you care to explain all this?

164
00:11:24,735 --> 00:11:27,614
Uh, w-well...

